de compr\u00e9hension","Accessible","Am\u00e9nagements pour les personnes aveugles et malvoyantes","Am\u00e9nagements pour personnes sourdes et malentendantes","Accessible aux pi\u00e9tons appareill\u00e9s","WC adapt\u00e9"],"nl":["Toegankelijk voor mensen met een verstandelijke beperking","Toegankelijk","Voorzieningen voor blinde en slechtziende personen","Voorzieningen voor dove en slechthorende personen","Toegankelijk voor voetgangers met hulpmiddelen","Aangepast toilet"],"en":["Accessible to people with intellectual disabilities","Accessible","Facilities for blind and partially-sighted persons","Facilities for deaf and hearing-impaired people","Accessible to pedestrians with mobility aids","Adapted toilet"]}},"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2022-05-18T01:06:44+02:00","published_at":"2021-09-14T10:33:03+02:00","backoffice_id":239024,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"expo","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.22131518264904},{"id":525797,"date_start":"2022-02-25","date_end":"2022-09-11","date_next":"2022-05-18","accept_article27":true,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition"}},"others":{"list":[36,47],"translations":{"fr":["Mus\u00e9es et art centers","Bande dessin\u00e9e"],"nl":["Musea en kunstcentra","Stripverhaal"],"en":["Museums and art centers","Comicstrip"]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr","nl","en"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Bulles de Louvre","shortdescr":"L\u2019exposition Bulles de Louvre, pr\u00e9sent\u00e9e au Mus\u00e9e de la BD, propose \u00e0 ses visiteurs de d\u00e9couvrir le Louvre \u00e0 travers le regard de vingt auteurs de bande dessin\u00e9e.","longdescr":"L\u2019exposition Bulles de Louvre, pr\u00e9sent\u00e9e au Mus\u00e9e de la BD, propose \u00e0 ses visiteurs de d\u00e9couvrir le Louvre \u00e0 travers le regard de vingt auteurs de Bande Dessin\u00e9e. En mettant en lumi\u00e8re chacun de leur univers et en explorant les th\u00e9matiques abord\u00e9es, l\u2019exposition montre comment ils se sont inspir\u00e9s de ce haut lieu culturel et des \u0153uvres pr\u00e9sentes pour imaginer des r\u00e9cits et partager leurs r\u00e9flexions sur l\u2019Art et la cr\u00e9ation.\r\nOrganis\u00e9e en partenariat avec le Mus\u00e9e du Louvre et les \u00e9ditions Futuropolis, l\u2019exposition pr\u00e9sente une collection \u00e9ditoriale qui donne carte blanche et acc\u00e8s aux salles du mus\u00e9e du Louvre \u00e0 des auteurs du Neuvi\u00e8me Art depuis 2005. Les artistes s\u2019approprient ce lieu embl\u00e9matique et se confrontent aux \u0153uvres pour livrer une interpr\u00e9tation graphique originale \u00e9dit\u00e9e en album.\r\nDe l\u2019Europe \u00e0 l\u2019Asie, de la bande dessin\u00e9e franco-belge au manga, l\u2019exposition invite \u00e0 un voyage entre les arts, les genres et les \u00e9poques. Vingt auteurs et pr\u00e8s de 150 \u0153uvres sont r\u00e9unies pour offrir aux visiteurs un parcours immersif dans leurs univers rythm\u00e9 par trois th\u00e9matiques principales.  Celles-ci mettent l\u2019accent sur la fa\u00e7on dont les auteurs revisitent l\u2019histoire du mus\u00e9e et des collections, comment ils en restituent le quotidien et observent les publics, et enfin comment ils sollicitent l\u2019expression po\u00e9tique pour magnifier les \u0153uvres.\r\nL\u2019exposition permet ainsi d\u2019appr\u00e9cier les cr\u00e9ations de Hirohiko Araki, Charles Berb\u00e9rian, Enki Bilal, Florent Chavouet, Nicolas De Cr\u00e9cy, Philippe Dupuy, Christian Durieux, Etienne Davodeau, Christian Lax, St\u00e9phane Levallois, Eric Liberge, Li Chi Tak, Marc-Antoine Mathieu, Taiyo Matsumoto, Minetar\u014d Mochizuki, David Prudhomme, Jiro Taniguchi, Naoki Urasawa, Bernard Yslaire et Judith Vanistendael. \u00c0 l\u2019image de la richesse des collections du Louvre, leurs \u0153uvres puissantes rendent compte de la diversit\u00e9 des styles et des perceptions, mais aussi d\u2019une approche sensible de l\u2019 l\u2019Art, de sa fonction et l\u2019universalit\u00e9 de son langage. \r\n\r\n\r\nCommissaires : M\u00e9lanie Andrieu & Fabrice Douar\r\n\r\nAvec la collaboration exceptionnel du Mus\u00e9e du Louvre\r\n\r\nAvec le soutien de la R\u00e9gion Bruxelles-Capitale, Visit Brussels, la F\u00e9d\u00e9ration Wallonie-Bruxelles et la Vlaamse Gemeenschapscommissie","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.cbbd.be\/fr\/expositions\/les-grandes-expositions-temporaires\/bulles-de-louvre","email":"visit@cbbd.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/fr\/detail\/id\/525797.html"},"nl":{"name":"Strips uit het Louvre","shortdescr":"De tentoonstelling Strips uit het Louvre, te zien in het Stripmuseum, nodigt zijn bezoekers uit het Louvre te herontdekken door de ogen van twintig stripauteurs.","longdescr":"De tentoonstelling Strips uit het Louvre, te zien in het Stripmuseum, nodigt zijn bezoekers uit het Louvre te herontdekken door de ogen van twintig stripauteurs. Door in te zoomen op elk van hun invalshoeken en op de aangesneden thema's toont de tentoonstelling hoe deze culturele trekpleister en zijn collecties hen inspireerde tot een waaier aan sterke verhalen en gedachten over Kunst en de creatie.  \r\nDe tentoonstelling, die groeide uit een samenwerking met het Museum het Louvre en uitgeverij Futuropolis, stelt een collectie voor die auteurs van de Negende Kunst carte blanche geeft, en onbeperke toegang tot de zalen van het Louvre. De artiesten maken zich deze iconische plek eigen en gaan de confrontatie aan met de werken die er hangen, om een originele grafische interpretatie af te leveren die wordt uitgegeven als album. \r\nVan Europa tot Azi\u00eb, van het Frans-Belgische stripverhaal tot de manga, nodigen de diverse artistieke creaties uit tot een nieuwe blik op verschillende kunsten, stromingen en tijdperken. Twintig auteurs en bijna 150 werken werden verzameld om bezoekers onder te dompelen in deze visies op het Louvre, met drie hoofdthema's. Auteurs duiken in de geschiedenis van het museum en zijn collecties, scheppen een beeld van het dagelijks leven en de bezoekers, of ze laten zich po\u00ebtisch inspireren door de werken om hun grootsheid nog in de verf te zetten.\r\nDe tentoonstelling verzamelt werken van Hirohiko Araki, Charles Berb\u00e9rian, Enki Bilal, Florent Chavouet, Nicolas De Cr\u00e9cy, Philippe Dupuy, Christian Durieux, Etienne Davodeau, Christian Lax, St\u00e9phane Levallois, Eric Liberge, Li Chi Tak, Marc-Antoine Mathieu, Taiyo Matsumoto, Minetar\u014d Mochizuki, David Prudhomme, Jiro Taniguchi, Naoki Urasawa, Bernard Yslaire en Judith Vanistendael. Hun pakkende verhalen, die in al hun diversiteit ook de rijkdom van de collecties van het museum weerspiegelen, getuigen van de verschillende stijlen en invalshoeken die zo eigen zijn aan de kunsten, maar ook van een gevoelige benadering van Kunst, haar rol in de maatschappij en haar universele beeldtaal.\r\n \r\n\r\nCuratoren : M\u00e9lanie Andrieu & Fabrice Douar\r\n\r\nMet de bijzondere samenwerking van het Museum het Louvre \r\n\r\nMet de steun van het Brussels Hoofdstedelijk Gewest, Visit Brussels, F\u00e9d\u00e9ration Wallonie-Bruxelles en de Vlaamse Gemeenschapscommissie","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.stripmuseum.be\/nl\/tentoonstellingen\/tijdelijke-tentoonstellingen\/strips-uit-het-louvre","email":"visit@stripmuseum.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/nl\/detail\/id\/525797.html"},"en":{"name":"Comics at the Louvre","shortdescr":"The exhibition Comics at the Louvre, presented by the Comics Art Museum, invites visitors to rediscover the Louvre through the works of twenty reknown comic strip artists.","longdescr":"The exhibition Comics at the Louvre, presented by the Comics Art Museum, invites visitors to rediscover the Louvre through the works of twenty reknown comic strip artists. In focusing on each universe and the different thematic angles the exhibition shows how this cultural hotspot and its collections inspired them for a variety of powerful narratives and thoughts on Art and creation.  \r\nThe exhibition, which stems from a partnership with the Louvre and publishing house Futuropolis, introduces a collection that invites comic artists and offers them a carte blanche as well as unlimited access to the galleries at the Louvre. The artists incorporate these iconic rooms and confront the works they meet, in order to give rise to unique graphic interpretations that are published as comic albums. \r\nFrom Europe to Asia, from French-Belgian bande dessin\u00e9e to manga, each of these diverse creations allows for a new view on different art forms, genres and eras. Twenty artists and about 150 works of art have been collected in one spot in order to immerse visitors in all of these approaches of the Louvre, which can be resumed to three main themes. Artists explore the history of the museum and its collections, they recreate daily life in the footsteps of the many visitors and staff, or they unleash their poetic imagination to magnify the works of art.\r\nThe exhibition proposes an overview of the works of Hirohiko Araki, Charles Berb\u00e9rian, Enki Bilal, Florent Chavouet, Nicolas De Cr\u00e9cy, Philippe Dupuy, Christian Durieux, Etienne Davodeau, Christian Lax, St\u00e9phane Levallois, Eric Liberge, Li Chi Tak, Marc-Antoine Mathieu, Taiyo Matsumoto, Minetar\u014d Mochizuki, David Prudhomme, Jiro Taniguchi, Naoki Urasawa, Bernard Yslaire and Judith Vanistendael. Their strong stories reflect the richness and diversity of the museum's collections and are born from sensitive approaches filled with reflections on Art, its function and its universal language. \r\n \r\n\r\nCurators : M\u00e9lanie Andrieu & Fabrice Douar\r\n\r\nWith the exceptional cooperation of the Louvre Museum \r\n\r\nWith the support of the Brussels Capital Region, Visit Brussels, F\u00e9d\u00e9ration Wallonie-Bruxelles and the Vlaamse Gemeenschapscommissie","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.comicscenter.net\/en\/exhibitions\/the-great-temporary-exhibitions\/comics-at-the-louvre","email":"visit@comicscenter.net","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/en\/detail\/id\/525797.html"},"de":{"name":"Bulles de Louvre","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/de\/detail\/id\/525797.html"},"it":{"name":"Bulles de Louvre","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/it\/detail\/id\/525797.html"},"sp":{"name":"Bulles de Louvre","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/sp\/detail\/id\/525797.html"},"pt":{"name":"Bulles de Louvre","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/pt\/detail\/id\/525797.html"},"cn":{"name":"Bulles de Louvre","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/cn\/detail\/id\/525797.html"}},"place":{"id":202864,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e de la Bande Dessin\u00e9e","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@cbbd.be","website":"http:\/\/www.cbbd.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Attraction incontournable situ\u00e9e au c\u0153ur de Bruxelles, le mus\u00e9e de la BD met \u00e0 l'honneur depuis plus de 25 ans auteurs et h\u00e9ros du 9\u00e8me Art. \r\n\r\nLes expositions permanentes r\u00e9guli\u00e8rement renouvel\u00e9es et un vaste programme d'expositions temporaires am\u00e8nent les visiteurs \u00e0 d\u00e9couvrir les innombrables facettes de la bande dessin\u00e9e. Tintin et les Schtroumpfs ouvrent la voie vers d'autres aventures, \u00e0 la rencontre d'un monde dont la cr\u00e9ativit\u00e9 n'a aucune limite. \r\n\r\nMagnifi\u00e9 par un exceptionnel cadre Art Nouveau con\u00e7u par Victor Horta, le Mus\u00e9e de la Bande Dessin\u00e9e est tout autant un hommage aux pionniers qu'un regard sur la BD actuelle.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Stripmuseum","address_street_name":"Zandstraat","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@stripmuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.stripmuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Zandstraat, 20","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Het Stripmuseum is voor al wie Brussel bezoekt een \u2018must\u2019 in het hartje van de stad. Al meer dan 25 jaar richt het museum de spots op de auteurs en de helden van de Negende Kunst. \r\n\r\nAan de hand van permanente tentoonstellingen \u2013 die regelmatig vernieuwd worden \u2013 en een afwisselend programma van tijdelijke exposities kan je er als bezoeker kennismaken met de talrijke facetten van het stripverhaal. Kuifje en de Smurfen nemen je mee naar avonturenland, een wereld waar de creativiteit geen grenzen kent. \r\n\r\nHet uitzonderlijke art nouveau-gebouw van Victor Horta geeft een bezoek nog een extra dimensie. Het Stripmuseum is tegelijk een hommage aan de pioniers van het medium als een blik op het hedendaagse stripverhaal.\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"The Belgian Comic Strip Center","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@comicscenter.net","website":"http:\/\/www.comicscenter.net\/en\/home","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"An accomplished attraction located in the heart of Brussels, the Belgian Comic Strip Center has been honouring the creators and heroes of the 9th Art for more than 25 years.\r\n\r\nThe regularly renewed permanent exhibitions and a diversified programme of temporary exhibitions enable visitors to discover the countless aspects of comics art. Tintin and the Smurfs lead the way towards further adventures, an encounter with a world where creativity has no limits. \r\n\r\nEnhanced by an exceptional Art Nouveau home designed by Victor Horta, the Belgian Comic Strip Center is just as much a tribute to the pioneers as a glimpse of contemporary comics art.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Comic-Museum - Centre Belge de la Bande Dessin\u00e9e","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@cbbd.be","website":"https:\/\/www.comicscenter.net\/en\/other-languages","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Br\u00fcssel als Comic-Hauptstadt g\u00f6nnt sich den Luxus eines eigenen Comic-Museums - das \u201eCentre Belge de la Bande Dessin\u00e9e\u201c. In einem eindrucksvollen Jugendstil-Bau aus der Feder von Victor Horta wird belgische und internationale Comic-Kunst pr\u00e4sentiert. Willkommen im Reich der Schl\u00fcmpfe, bei Tim und Struppi, Lucky Luke, Spirou, Gaston Lagaffe und all den anderen Comic-Helden!\r\n\r\nComic-Kunst und Jugendstilarchitektur: Der ber\u00fchmte Jugendstilarchitekt Victor Horta entwarf 1903, auf dem H\u00f6hepunkt seines Schaffens, Pl\u00e4ne f\u00fcr ein weitl\u00e4ufiges Bauwerk in Br\u00fcssel. Nach der Renovierung 1989 lie\u00df sich in den R\u00e4umen, die in allen Bereichen durch Jugendstilelemente gepr\u00e4gt sind, das \u201eCentre Belge de la Bande Dessin\u00e9e\", das Belgische Comiczentrum nieder, bei dem sich auf einer Fl\u00e4che von mehr als 4000 m\u00b2 - von den Urspr\u00fcngen bis hin zu avantgardistischen Werken - alles um Comics dreht.\r\n\r\nBelgische Comic-Kunst in all ihren Formen: Ausstellungen, Konferenzen, Kreativ-Workshops, Veranstaltungen, eine eigene Comic-Bibliothek mit Dokumentationszentrum sowie eine gut sortierte Buchhandlung bilden ein vielseitiges und buntes Comicangebot. Zentrale Themen der Dauerausstellung sind die Erfindung der Comic-Kunst, die Formen und die Entwicklung der Comic-Kunst sowie verschiedene Schwerpunkt auf belgische Comic-K\u00fcnstler von Peyo, dem Vater der Schl\u00fcmpfe bis Herg\u00e9, dem Erfinder von Tim & Struppi.\r\n\r\nComic-Fans auf zum Br\u00fcsseler Comic-Mekka!","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Museo del Fumetto","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@comicscenter.net","website":"https:\/\/www.comicscenter.net\/en\/other-languages","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Il Museo del Fumetto CBBD, situato nel cuore storico di Bruxelles, riunisce su pi\u00f9 di 4.000 m\u00b2 tutto ci\u00f2 che riguarda il fumetto. Ospitato in un edificio tempio dell'Art Nouveau disegnato da Victor Horta, il museo \u00e8 il regno di celebri eroi dei fumetti belgi: Tintin, i Puffi, Lucky Luke, Gaston Lagaffe, Blake et Mortimer, Marsupilami... Le esposizioni organizzate, la biblioteca e il centro di documentazione, non solo rendono il museo vivo e dinamico, ma sono veri e propri centri di documentazione sul fumetto il cuicatalogo \u00e8 accessibile on-line. Il centro belga del fumetto organizza conferenze, laboratori creativi ed animazioni, ecc.\r\n\r\n\r\nAperto i giorni festivi eccetto il 25\/12 e 01\/01. Il Centro Belga del Fumetto diverse formule di visita: la visita guidata del museo, quella del Percorso del Fumetto o quella del museo Marc Sleen. Il museo, anzi il centro belga del fumetto-CBBD ospita anche una brasserie dove potete respirare l'inconfondibile atmosfera di Bruxelles.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Centro belga del c\u00f3mic (CBBD)","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@comicscenter.net","website":"https:\/\/www.comicscenter.net\/en\/other-languages","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Ubicado en el centro de Bruselas, en un edificio Art Nouveau construido por Victor Horta en 1906, el CBBD abri\u00f3 sus puertas el 6 de octubre de 1989. \r\n\r\nEn pocos a\u00f1os, este museo se ha convertido en una de las principales atracciones de Bruselas. \r\n\r\nCada a\u00f1o, m\u00e1s de 200.000 visitantes recorren las exposiciones permanentes y temporales que se celebran en m\u00e1s de 4.000 m 2. \r\n\r\nAunque las exposiciones contribuyen a convertir este templo en un lugar viviente, din\u00e1mico y atrayente, esta herramienta al servicio de la promoci\u00f3n del c\u00f3mic constituye un centro de documentaci\u00f3n moderno, con un cat\u00e1logo accesible online. \r\n\r\nTambi\u00e9n se llevan a cabo conferencias y talleres creativos.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"O Centro Belga da Banda Desenhada","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@cbbd.be","website":"http:\/\/www.cbbd.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Atra\u00e7\u00e3o incontorn\u00e1vel situada no centro de Bruxelas, o museu da BD comemora mais de 25 anos de autores e her\u00f3is da 9.\u00aa arte.\r\nAs exposi\u00e7\u00f5es permanentes regularmente renovadas e um vasto programa de exposi\u00e7\u00f5es tempor\u00e1rias levam os visitantes a descobrir as in\u00fameras facetas da banda desenhada. Tintim e os Estrumpfes abrem a porta a outras aventuras, ao encontro de um mundo onde a criatividade n\u00e3o tem limites. \r\nAmpliado por uma moldura invulgar Arte Nouveau concebida por Victor Horta, o Museu da Banda Desenhada \u00e9 tanto uma homenagem aos pioneiros que um olhar sobre a BD atual.\r\nAberto todos os dias das 10 \u00e0s 18 horas.\r\nEntrada gratuita apenas com o Brussels Card \u201c100masters\u201d","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"The Belgian Comic Strip Center","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@cbbd.be","website":"http:\/\/www.cbbd.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":[],"zones":{"list":[19],"translations":{"fr":["Centre"],"nl":["Centrum"],"en":["Centre"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":405,"location":{"lat":50.85107181,"lon":4.36006874},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-05-18T01:07:03+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:30+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":202864,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e de la Bande Dessin\u00e9e","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@cbbd.be","website":"http:\/\/www.cbbd.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Attraction incontournable situ\u00e9e au c\u0153ur de Bruxelles, le mus\u00e9e de la BD met \u00e0 l'honneur depuis plus de 25 ans auteurs et h\u00e9ros du 9\u00e8me Art. \r\n\r\nLes expositions permanentes r\u00e9guli\u00e8rement renouvel\u00e9es et un vaste programme d'expositions temporaires am\u00e8nent les visiteurs \u00e0 d\u00e9couvrir les innombrables facettes de la bande dessin\u00e9e. Tintin et les Schtroumpfs ouvrent la voie vers d'autres aventures, \u00e0 la rencontre d'un monde dont la cr\u00e9ativit\u00e9 n'a aucune limite. \r\n\r\nMagnifi\u00e9 par un exceptionnel cadre Art Nouveau con\u00e7u par Victor Horta, le Mus\u00e9e de la Bande Dessin\u00e9e est tout autant un hommage aux pionniers qu'un regard sur la BD actuelle.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Stripmuseum","address_street_name":"Zandstraat","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@stripmuseum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.stripmuseum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Zandstraat, 20","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Het Stripmuseum is voor al wie Brussel bezoekt een \u2018must\u2019 in het hartje van de stad. Al meer dan 25 jaar richt het museum de spots op de auteurs en de helden van de Negende Kunst. \r\n\r\nAan de hand van permanente tentoonstellingen \u2013 die regelmatig vernieuwd worden \u2013 en een afwisselend programma van tijdelijke exposities kan je er als bezoeker kennismaken met de talrijke facetten van het stripverhaal. Kuifje en de Smurfen nemen je mee naar avonturenland, een wereld waar de creativiteit geen grenzen kent. \r\n\r\nHet uitzonderlijke art nouveau-gebouw van Victor Horta geeft een bezoek nog een extra dimensie. Het Stripmuseum is tegelijk een hommage aan de pioniers van het medium als een blik op het hedendaagse stripverhaal.\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"The Belgian Comic Strip Center","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@comicscenter.net","website":"http:\/\/www.comicscenter.net\/en\/home","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"An accomplished attraction located in the heart of Brussels, the Belgian Comic Strip Center has been honouring the creators and heroes of the 9th Art for more than 25 years.\r\n\r\nThe regularly renewed permanent exhibitions and a diversified programme of temporary exhibitions enable visitors to discover the countless aspects of comics art. Tintin and the Smurfs lead the way towards further adventures, an encounter with a world where creativity has no limits. \r\n\r\nEnhanced by an exceptional Art Nouveau home designed by Victor Horta, the Belgian Comic Strip Center is just as much a tribute to the pioneers as a glimpse of contemporary comics art.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Comic-Museum - Centre Belge de la Bande Dessin\u00e9e","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@cbbd.be","website":"https:\/\/www.comicscenter.net\/en\/other-languages","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Br\u00fcssel als Comic-Hauptstadt g\u00f6nnt sich den Luxus eines eigenen Comic-Museums - das \u201eCentre Belge de la Bande Dessin\u00e9e\u201c. In einem eindrucksvollen Jugendstil-Bau aus der Feder von Victor Horta wird belgische und internationale Comic-Kunst pr\u00e4sentiert. Willkommen im Reich der Schl\u00fcmpfe, bei Tim und Struppi, Lucky Luke, Spirou, Gaston Lagaffe und all den anderen Comic-Helden!\r\n\r\nComic-Kunst und Jugendstilarchitektur: Der ber\u00fchmte Jugendstilarchitekt Victor Horta entwarf 1903, auf dem H\u00f6hepunkt seines Schaffens, Pl\u00e4ne f\u00fcr ein weitl\u00e4ufiges Bauwerk in Br\u00fcssel. Nach der Renovierung 1989 lie\u00df sich in den R\u00e4umen, die in allen Bereichen durch Jugendstilelemente gepr\u00e4gt sind, das \u201eCentre Belge de la Bande Dessin\u00e9e\", das Belgische Comiczentrum nieder, bei dem sich auf einer Fl\u00e4che von mehr als 4000 m\u00b2 - von den Urspr\u00fcngen bis hin zu avantgardistischen Werken - alles um Comics dreht.\r\n\r\nBelgische Comic-Kunst in all ihren Formen: Ausstellungen, Konferenzen, Kreativ-Workshops, Veranstaltungen, eine eigene Comic-Bibliothek mit Dokumentationszentrum sowie eine gut sortierte Buchhandlung bilden ein vielseitiges und buntes Comicangebot. Zentrale Themen der Dauerausstellung sind die Erfindung der Comic-Kunst, die Formen und die Entwicklung der Comic-Kunst sowie verschiedene Schwerpunkt auf belgische Comic-K\u00fcnstler von Peyo, dem Vater der Schl\u00fcmpfe bis Herg\u00e9, dem Erfinder von Tim & Struppi.\r\n\r\nComic-Fans auf zum Br\u00fcsseler Comic-Mekka!","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Museo del Fumetto","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@comicscenter.net","website":"https:\/\/www.comicscenter.net\/en\/other-languages","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Il Museo del Fumetto CBBD, situato nel cuore storico di Bruxelles, riunisce su pi\u00f9 di 4.000 m\u00b2 tutto ci\u00f2 che riguarda il fumetto. Ospitato in un edificio tempio dell'Art Nouveau disegnato da Victor Horta, il museo \u00e8 il regno di celebri eroi dei fumetti belgi: Tintin, i Puffi, Lucky Luke, Gaston Lagaffe, Blake et Mortimer, Marsupilami... Le esposizioni organizzate, la biblioteca e il centro di documentazione, non solo rendono il museo vivo e dinamico, ma sono veri e propri centri di documentazione sul fumetto il cuicatalogo \u00e8 accessibile on-line. Il centro belga del fumetto organizza conferenze, laboratori creativi ed animazioni, ecc.\r\n\r\n\r\nAperto i giorni festivi eccetto il 25\/12 e 01\/01. Il Centro Belga del Fumetto diverse formule di visita: la visita guidata del museo, quella del Percorso del Fumetto o quella del museo Marc Sleen. Il museo, anzi il centro belga del fumetto-CBBD ospita anche una brasserie dove potete respirare l'inconfondibile atmosfera di Bruxelles.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Centro belga del c\u00f3mic (CBBD)","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@comicscenter.net","website":"https:\/\/www.comicscenter.net\/en\/other-languages","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Ubicado en el centro de Bruselas, en un edificio Art Nouveau construido por Victor Horta en 1906, el CBBD abri\u00f3 sus puertas el 6 de octubre de 1989. \r\n\r\nEn pocos a\u00f1os, este museo se ha convertido en una de las principales atracciones de Bruselas. \r\n\r\nCada a\u00f1o, m\u00e1s de 200.000 visitantes recorren las exposiciones permanentes y temporales que se celebran en m\u00e1s de 4.000 m 2. \r\n\r\nAunque las exposiciones contribuyen a convertir este templo en un lugar viviente, din\u00e1mico y atrayente, esta herramienta al servicio de la promoci\u00f3n del c\u00f3mic constituye un centro de documentaci\u00f3n moderno, con un cat\u00e1logo accesible online. \r\n\r\nTambi\u00e9n se llevan a cabo conferencias y talleres creativos.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"O Centro Belga da Banda Desenhada","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@cbbd.be","website":"http:\/\/www.cbbd.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Atra\u00e7\u00e3o incontorn\u00e1vel situada no centro de Bruxelas, o museu da BD comemora mais de 25 anos de autores e her\u00f3is da 9.\u00aa arte.\r\nAs exposi\u00e7\u00f5es permanentes regularmente renovadas e um vasto programa de exposi\u00e7\u00f5es tempor\u00e1rias levam os visitantes a descobrir as in\u00fameras facetas da banda desenhada. Tintim e os Estrumpfes abrem a porta a outras aventuras, ao encontro de um mundo onde a criatividade n\u00e3o tem limites. \r\nAmpliado por uma moldura invulgar Arte Nouveau concebida por Victor Horta, o Museu da Banda Desenhada \u00e9 tanto uma homenagem aos pioneiros que um olhar sobre a BD atual.\r\nAberto todos os dias das 10 \u00e0s 18 horas.\r\nEntrada gratuita apenas com o Brussels Card \u201c100masters\u201d","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"The Belgian Comic Strip Center","address_street_name":"Rue des Sables","address_street_number":"20","address_street_box":null,"email":"visit@cbbd.be","website":"http:\/\/www.cbbd.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 19 80","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue des Sables, 20","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":405,"location":{"lat":50.85107181,"lon":4.36006874},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-05-18T01:07:03+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:30+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"poster","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels.imgix.net\/0a5e0d17ccc6799ea052351b0dd4bd7e3c5932f9.jpg","width":4961,"height":7016,"ratio":0.71,"translations":{"fr":{"title":"Bulles de Louvre","copyright":null},"nl":{"title":"Bulles de Louvre","copyright":null},"en":{"title":"Bulles de Louvre","copyright":null}}},{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels.imgix.net\/b1bc1a48144010a568767e7e39ebdd974995dda6.jpg","width":1500,"height":1000,"ratio":1.5,"translations":{"fr":{"title":"Bulles de Louvre","copyright":"Daniel Fouss \/ CBBD"},"nl":{"title":"Bulles de Louvre","copyright":"Daniel Fouss \/ BSC"},"en":{"title":"Bulles de Louvre","copyright":"Daniel Fouss \/ Comics Art Museum"}}},{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels.imgix.net\/b41a99da5816bd8a6af2e95ddca9ba0400da7e6d.jpg","width":1500,"height":1000,"ratio":1.5,"translations":{"fr":{"title":"Bu