n Brusselse geschiedenis en cultuur! \r\nHet Koninklijk Theater Toone zet sinds 1830 de eeuwenoude traditie van het volkse Theater voort.\r\nDe programmatie is gebaseerd op grote toneelklassiekers zoals \"Cyrano de Bergerac\" van Edmond Rostand, \"De Drie Musketiers\" van Alexandre Dumas, \"Romeo en Julia\" van William Shakespeare en \"Tijl Uilenspiegel\" van Charles De Coster. \r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Th\u00e9\u00e2tre Royal de Toone","address_street_name":"Rue du March\u00e9 aux Herbes","address_street_number":"66","address_street_box":null,"email":"woltje@skynet.be","website":"http:\/\/www.toone.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 511 71 37","phone_booking":"+32 2 513 54 86","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Rue du March\u00e9 aux Herbes, 66","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"During the Spanish occupation of the Netherlands all theaters were closed to prevent the actors from raising satirical pieces against the Spanish rulers. As a result, doll shows came into play: it was easier to tolerate the fierce dialogues when pronounced by lifeless dolls. About 1830 Antoine \"Toone\" Genty opened  a puppet theater, then in the Marolles. More than 180 years later, this popular entertainment has grown into a Royal Puppet Theater. After Genty, his (unrelated) successors would also be called Toone (Antoine).\r\nThe classics are performed in the local Brussels dialect with wooden puppets (the so-called poechenel), sometimes in Dutch or in French. The puppet theater and museum has been located near the Grand Place for four decades. The theater is located on the upper floors of the building, on the ground floor there is a pub. The museum contains old dolls, including 19th century specimens.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Marionettentheater - Th\u00e9\u00e2tre Royal de Toone","address_street_name":"Rue du March\u00e9 aux Herbes","address_street_number":"66","address_street_box":null,"email":"woltje@skynet.be","website":"http:\/\/www.toone.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 511 71 37","phone_booking":"+32 2 513 54 86","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du March\u00e9 aux Herbes, 66","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"W\u00e4hrend der spanischen Besetzung der Niederlande wurden zwangsweise s\u00e4mtliche Theater geschlossen, um Kritik - in Form von satirischen St\u00fccken - an den spanischen Herrschern zu unterbinden. Die Br\u00fcsseler haben alsdann die Schauspieler durch Marionetten (\"Poechenelles\" in Br\u00fcsseler Mundart) ersetzt, die in illegalen Theatern auftragen. \r\nAnfang des 19. Jahrhunderts z\u00e4hlten die Br\u00fcsseler Marionettentheater zu den beliebtesten Vergn\u00fcgungen f\u00fcr Erwachsene, denn sie boten eine enorme Freiheit, ben\u00f6tigen nur wenig finanzielle Mittel und konnten \u00fcberall aufgef\u00fchrt werden. Ihr Repertoire ist bis heute sehr vielf\u00e4ltig und reicht von volkst\u00fcmlichen Legenden \u00fcber Rittergeschichten bis hin zu religi\u00f6sen oder historischen St\u00fccken, die sehr frei interpretiert werden. \r\nSeit der Gr\u00fcndung des Theaters im Marollenviertel ist nun bereits die 9. Puppenspielergeneration der Toone-Dynastie am Werk. Der jeweils neue Toone (Br\u00fcsseler Kosename f\u00fcr \"Antoine\", so der Vorname des Gr\u00fcnders) muss sowohl von seinem Vorg\u00e4nger als auch von dem Publikum angenommen werden - und so ist es nicht unbedingt der jeweilige Sohn, der die Nachfolge antritt. \r\nDie Klassiker werden in Br\u00fcsseler Mundart und manchmal auch auf Niederl\u00e4ndisch oder Franz\u00f6sisch aufgef\u00fchrt. \r\nDas Th\u00e9\u00e2tre de Toone birgt auch ein urige Schenke und ein Marionettenmuseum.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Teatro Reale di Toone VII","address_street_name":"Rue du March\u00e9 aux Herbes","address_street_number":"66","address_street_box":null,"email":"woltje@skynet.be","website":"http:\/\/www.toone.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 511 71 37","phone_booking":"+32 2 513 54 86","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du March\u00e9 aux Herbes, 66","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Traditional Brussels\u2019 puppet theater & museum - Typical caf\u00e9\r\nBordering the Impasses Schuddeveld and Sainte-P\u00e9tronille, you will find one of the favourite places of Brussels citizens: Le th\u00e9\u00e2tre de Toone.\r\nTheater Toone is simultaneously a typical estaminet with its Spanish pink brick walls, blackened beams and tiled floor, a puppet theatre in the attic, with its wooden benches, festooned, multicoloured cushions nailed into the raw wood planks and a puppet museum. There, we find the characters who retired from the stage, these Toone heroes of the past and fetish characters of fellow puppeteers from around the world.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Teatro Real Toone VII","address_street_name":"Rue du March\u00e9 aux Herbes","address_street_number":"66","address_street_box":null,"email":"woltje@skynet.be","website":"http:\/\/www.toone.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 511 71 37","phone_booking":"+32 2 513 54 86","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du March\u00e9 aux Herbes, 66","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Th\u00e9\u00e2tre Royal de Toone","address_street_name":"Rue du March\u00e9 aux Herbes - Entr\u00e9e : Impasse Sainte P\u00e9tronille","address_street_number":"66","address_street_box":null,"email":"woltje@skynet.be","website":"http:\/\/www.toone.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 511 71 37","phone_booking":"+32 2 513 54 86","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1"