\/\/agenda.brussels\/fr\/detail\/id\/533691.html"},"nl":{"name":"REVERS (et autres tendresses de l'oubli)","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/nl\/detail\/id\/533691.html"},"en":{"name":"REVERS (et autres tendresses de l'oubli)","shortdescr":"The gallery is very happy to welcome for the 1st time the work of Babette Goossens.\r\nHer paintings and videos are worth the view.\r\nThe subtle subjects she has picked are exquisite, sensible and made with great attention to details.","longdescr":"\"When I paint, words come to mind.\r\ntenderness\r\nrepentance\r\njockey carcass\r\nbark Lady\r\npeels\r\nseptentrional\r\nshroud\r\noranges\r\ntender\r\nlead\r\nvanity zest and lemon ...\r\nmirage\r\n\r\nI assemble them mentally until they resonate with my painting, in harmony with the image, the atmosphere or the pictorial material.\r\nLittle by little I compose titles, intended to name (or nourish) such a painting, such another drawing, a video, a new series of works or an upcoming exhibition...\r\nThe words form an echo. Suggest, evoke. Perhaps something else than the image. A gap.\r\nA doubt. An uncertainty. A shift, a witticism. Perhaps they are a clue?\r\nWords amuse me when they allow me to reveal a lead by blurring it.\r\nWe must observe the gaps and the silences.\r\nTo say half a word.\r\nThe works say half a word, the words say something else.\r\nREVERS is not only the reverse or the unfortunate event, it is also (in french) the plural of dream.\r\nAt first glance, forgetting does not look tender; but isn't it, in the end? \"","performers":"Babette Goossens","boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/en\/detail\/id\/533691.html"},"de":{"name":"REVERS (et autres tendresses de l'oubli)","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,