n":{"name":"Normal"}},"value":26},{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Senior"},"nl":{"name":"Senioren"},"en":{"name":"Senior"}},"value":23},{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Jeunes"},"nl":{"name":"Jongeren"},"en":{"name":"Young"}},"value":9},{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Demandeurs d'emploi"},"nl":{"name":"Werkzoekenden"},"en":{"name":"Jobseekers"}},"value":10},{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Article 27"},"nl":{"name":"Artikel 27"},"en":{"name":"Article 27"}},"value":1.25}],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":[],"accessibilities":[],"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2022-05-18T01:35:26+02:00","published_at":"2021-06-07T16:44:28+02:00","backoffice_id":232747,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"theatre","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.48074985676914},{"id":518822,"date_start":"2021-10-22","date_end":"2022-05-29","date_next":"2022-05-18","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition"}},"others":{"list":[36,40],"translations":{"fr":["Mus\u00e9es et art centers","Arts graphiques"],"nl":["Musea en kunstcentra","Grafische kunst, vormgeving"],"en":["Museums and art centers","Graphic art"]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr","nl","en"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Before Time Began","shortdescr":"L\u2019univers aborig\u00e8ne \u00e9merveille et intrigue. Aux yeux des non-initi\u00e9s, il est charg\u00e9 de myst\u00e8re. Les premiers habitants d\u2019Australie sont les h\u00e9ritiers depuis 65.000 ans de la plus ancienne culture ininterrompue au monde.","longdescr":"BEFORE TIME BEGAN explore le R\u00eave et la Cr\u00e9ation, mais aussi la naissance de l\u2019art contemporain. L\u2019exposition est construite autour de plusieurs moments de production artistique : quelques peintures traditionnelles sur \u00e9corce des ann\u00e9es 1950 (et au-del\u00e0) faisant usage de pigments naturels et en provenance de la Terre d\u2019Arnhem ; des travaux des r\u00e9gions d\u00e9sertiques des ann\u00e9es 1970 et du mouvement artistique naissant du d\u00e9sert occidental, o\u00f9 les artistes s\u2019essaient \u00e0 la couleur industrielle sur toile et sur panneau ; mais aussi les productions les plus r\u00e9centes, parfois monumentales, de divers artistes contemporains, individuelles ou collectives. Deux court-m\u00e9trages mettent en sc\u00e8ne un groupe de femmes et un autre d\u2019hommes, tous artistes et cr\u00e9ant des \u0153uvres collaboratives. Tandis qu\u2019ils s\u2019activent, ils racontent des histoires, chantent, rient et dansent. Si ce qui est r\u00e9serv\u00e9 aux initi\u00e9s ne se divulgue pas, les \u0153uvres d\u2019art illustrent des r\u00e9cits mythiques ancestraux et t\u00e9moignent d\u2019une connexion avec, et d\u2019un profond respect pour la terre et la nature.\r\n\r\nL\u2019exposition pr\u00e9sente en point de mire l\u2019installation Kulata Tjuta (Beaucoup de lances), cr\u00e9\u00e9e par un groupe d\u2019artistes de tous \u00e2ges issus de certains des centres artistiques des Terres APY (Anangu Pitjantjatjara Yankunytjatjara). Mille cinq cent lances sont agenc\u00e9es pour \u00e9voquer un kupi kupi, un tourbillon de poussi\u00e8re en forme d\u2019entonnoir comme ceux qui surviennent dans les r\u00e9gions d\u00e9sertiques.\r\n\r\nLa derni\u00e8re section de l\u2019exposition pr\u00e9sente le travail du photographe et artiste contemporain Michael Cook. Cook s\u2019int\u00e9resse \u00e0 l\u2019id\u00e9e de \u00ab civilisation \u00bb. Il expose sa s\u00e9rie Civilised, compos\u00e9e de photographies d\u2019Aborig\u00e8nes d\u2019Australie v\u00eatus de costumes historiques des puissances europ\u00e9ennes qui visit\u00e8rent l\u2019Australie au d\u00e9but de la colonisation.\r\n\r\nL\u2019exposition BEFORE TIME BEGAN s\u2019inscrit dans la nouvelle mission des Mus\u00e9es royaux d\u2019Art et d\u2019Histoire (MRAH) qui veulent susciter \u00e0 Bruxelles, au c\u0153ur de l\u2019Europe, la curiosit\u00e9 et l\u2019\u00e9merveillement pour la diversit\u00e9 des mondes et des univers cr\u00e9\u00e9s par les femmes et par les hommes. Les MRAH cr\u00e9ent des espaces de d\u00e9mocratisation, d\u2019inclusion et de diversit\u00e9 pour un dialogue critique sur le pass\u00e9 et l\u2019avenir. Ils cherchent \u00e0 approfondir leur connaissance de la soci\u00e9t\u00e9 et des cultures. Cela nous encourage tous \u00e0 prendre mieux soin du monde et \u00e0 s\u2019autoriser d\u00e8s lors \u00e0 imaginer un monde diff\u00e9rent. L\u2019exposition est une production de la Fondation Opale \u00e0 Lens (Suisse), Le plus important centre europ\u00e9en pour l\u2019art et la culture aborig\u00e8nes. Les \u0153uvres pr\u00e9sent\u00e9es dans BEFORE TIME BEGAN, dont la plupart viennent de cette collection, sont issues des contr\u00e9es isol\u00e9es d\u2019Australie et peuvent se targuer d\u2019un traitement \u00e9thiquement responsable.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","email":"info@mrah.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 741 73 02","agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/fr\/detail\/id\/518822.html"},"nl":{"name":"Before Time Began","shortdescr":"De wereld van de Aboriginals is wonderlijk en fascinerend, vol geheimen voor niet-ingewijden. De eerste inwoners van Australi\u00eb zijn de erfgenamen van de oudste ononderbroken cultuur ter wereld, die tot 65.000 jaar terug zou gaan.","longdescr":"BEFORE TIME BEGAN verwijst naar de Droom en de creatie van het land, maar ook naar het ontstaan van de hedendaagse kunst. De kern van de tentoonstelling is opgebouwd uit enkele klassieke schilderijen op boombast met natuurlijke pigmenten uit de jaren 1950 (en later) uit Arnhem Land, werken uit de jaren 1970 uit de woestijngebieden, wanneer de Western Desert schildersbeweging ontstond en kunstenaars gingen experimenteren met kleurige industri\u00eble verf op doek en paneel, maar ook de meest recente, soms monumentale, kunstuitingen van diverse hedendaagse kunstenaars, zowel individueel- als groepswerk. Twee korte filmpjes tonen een groep mannelijke en een groep vrouwelijke kunstenaars samenwerken. Er worden verhalen verteld, er wordt gezongen, gelachen en gedanst. Terwijl wat niet voor de ogen van niet-ingewijden bestemd is, onderliggend verborgen blijft, tonen de kunstwerken eeuwenoude mythische verhalen en getuigen van een verbondenheid met en een diep respect voor de aarde en de natuur.\r\n\r\nEen blikvanger in de tentoonstelling is de installatie Kulata Tjuta (vele speren), gecre\u00eberd door een groep oudere en jongere kunstenaars uit enkele APY (Anangu Pitjantjatjara Yankunytjatjara) Lands kunstcentra. Het werk is opgebouwd uit 1500 speren en stelt een kupi kupi, of stofwervelwind in trechtervorm voor, zoals die voorkomt in woestijngebieden. \r\n\r\nHet laatste luik van de tentoonstelling bestaat uit fotografisch werk van hedendaags kunstenaar Michael Cook. Hij reflecteert op de idee van beschaving en toont zo bv. in \u00e9\u00e9n van zijn fotoseries Civilised Aboriginal Australi\u00ebrs uitgedost in historische kledij van de Europese mogendheden die Australi\u00eb aan het begin van de kolonisatie bezochten.\r\n\r\nDe tentoonstelling past in de vernieuwde missie van de Koninklijke Musea voor Kunst en Geschiedenis (KMKG) om in Brussel, in het hart van Europa, nieuwsgierigheid en verwondering aan te wakkeren voor de werelden die vrouwen en mannen hebben gemaakt. De KMKG bieden democratiserende, inclusieve en meerstemmige ruimtes aan voor een kritische dialoog over verleden en toekomst. Ze streven diepere inzichten in samenleving en culturen na. Dat moedigt ons allen aan om beter zorg te dragen voor de wereld, waardoor we ons ook een andere wereld kunnen voorstellen. De tentoonstelling is oorspronkelijk een productie van de Fondation Opale in Lens (Zwitserland), Europa\u2019s belangrijkste centrum voor Aboriginal kunst en cultuur. De kunstwerken in BEFORE TIME BEGAN zijn afkomstig uit afgelegen gebieden in Australi\u00eb, ze werden op een correcte ethische wijze verworven en behoren grotendeels tot deze verzameling.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","email":"info@kmkg.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 741 73 02","agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/nl\/detail\/id\/518822.html"},"en":{"name":"Before Time Began","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"From 22 October 2021 to 29 May 2022, the Art & History Museum will be exhibiting Australian Aboriginal art for the first time. The world of the Aboriginals is a wonderful and fascinating universe, filled with secrets for the non-initiated. The First Peoples of Australia are the heirs to the oldest continuous culture in the world, which dates back 65.000 years. However rich, this culture is not expressed in architecture, written texts or artefacts. Today, as in the past, ancestral knowledge is exclusively passed on from one generation to the next by means of an oral tradition centred around rituals and ceremonies, in which the concept of \u2018Dreamings\u2019 or \u2018Dreamtime\u2019 plays a vital role.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","email":"info@mrah.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 741 73 02","agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/en\/detail\/id\/518822.html"},"de":{"name":"Before Time Began","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/de\/detail\/id\/518822.html"},"it":{"name":"Before Time Began","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/it\/detail\/id\/518822.html"},"sp":{"name":"Before Time Began","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/sp\/detail\/id\/518822.html"},"pt":{"name":"Before Time Began","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/pt\/detail\/id\/518822.html"},"cn":{"name":"Before Time Began","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/cn\/detail\/id\/518822.html"}},"place":{"id":61,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e Art & Histoire (MRAH)","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@mrah.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 15","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"De l'arch\u00e9ologie nationale aux arts d\u00e9coratifs europ\u00e9ens en passant par l'Antiquit\u00e9 classique et les civilisations non europ\u00e9ennes, embarquez pour un fascinant voyage \u00e0 travers l'art et l'histoire dans un magnifique b\u00e2timent, cr\u00e9\u00e9 par L\u00e9opold II dans le parc du Cinquantenaire \u00e0 Bruxelles.\r\n\r\nLe Mus\u00e9e Art & Histoire fait partie des Mus\u00e9es royaux d\u2019Art et d\u2019Histoire, appellation qui chapeaute, outre le Mus\u00e9e Art & Histoire, le mim (Mus\u00e9e des Instruments de Musique), la Porte de Hal et les Mus\u00e9es d\u2019Extr\u00eame-Orient actuellement ferm\u00e9s. ","description_print":"Le Mus\u00e9e du Cinquantenaire illustre les activit\u00e9s humaines et artistiques des cinq continents \u2013 hormis l\u2019Afrique noire \u2013, de la Pr\u00e9histoire \u00e0 nos jours. Les collections remplissent quatre b\u00e2timents et sont regroup\u00e9es en quatre d\u00e9partements: l\u2019Antiquit\u00e9, les civilisations extra-europ\u00e9ennes, l\u2019arch\u00e9ologie nationale et les arts d\u00e9coratifs europ\u00e9ens.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Museum Kunst & Geschiedenis (KMKG)","address_street_name":"Jubelpark","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kmkg.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 14","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Jubelpark","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Maak een wereldreis door de geschiedenis! Wandel van prehistorische vuistbijlen naar Egyptische mummies. Snuistert tussen betoverende glas en zet een stap achteruit om de indrukwekkende Brusselse wandtapijten te bekijken. Ga de oosterse toer op tussen de Aziatische boeddha\u2019s en steek de Atlantische Oceaan over om Kuifjes \u2018beeldje met het gebroken oor\u2019. En dan is er nog de mooie collectie van Belgische art nouveau\u2026 U komt ogen en oren te kort!\r\n\r\nHet Museum Kunst & Geschiedenis maakt deel uit van de Koninklijke Musea voor Kunst en Geschiedenis (KMKG) die ook het Muziekinstrumentenmuseum (MIM), de Hallepoort en de Musea van het Verre Oosten (gesloten voor renovatie) bundelen.","description_print":"Het Jubelparkmuseum kan bogen op een imposante collectie kunstschatten en archeologische vondsten afkomstig uit de vijf continenten \u2013 met uitzondering van Zwart-Afrika \u2013 van de prehistorie tot op heden. De verzamelingen vullen vier gebouwen en zijn ingedeeld in evenveel departementen: Oudheid (het Nabije Oosten, Egypte, Griekenland, Rome en Byzantium), Niet-Europese Beschavingen (Islam, Azi\u00eb, Polynesi\u00eb & Micronesi\u00eb en Amerika), Nationale Archeologie en Europese Sierkunsten.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Art & History Museum (RMAH)","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@mrah.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 14","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"Step inside this historic building, one of the biggest museums in Belgium and erected by former Belgian King Leopold II. Discover a wealth of artefacts from prehistoric times over antiquity and the European applied arts to a vast collection of non-European art. Explore what's on, including interesting temporary exhibitions, lectures and various other activities. Unfortunately, the website does not extend to giving you a full viewing of our collection, comprising thousands of art treasures and historical objects. However, we hope that you will come and visit us and enjoy discovering or rediscovering the immense heritage that we manage and display. To us, indeed, art and history are not dead and dusty subjects, but very much alive and a constant source of inspiration and enjoyment.\r\n\r\nThe Art & History Museum is part of the Royal Museums of Art and History (RMAH) that also cover the Musical Instruments Museum (MIM), Halle Gate and the Museums of the Far East (currently closed for renovation).","description_print":"The Cinquantenaire Museum is the headquarters of the Royal Museums of Art and History. It was erected at the end of the nineteenth century and is one of the most extensive museums in Belgium. The collections are divided according to four main themes: 1) National Archaeology; 2) Antiquity; 3) European Decorative Art; 4) Non-European Civilizations.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e Art & Histoire (MRAH)","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@mrah.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 14","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Das Cinquantenaire-Museum, gelegen im Br\u00fcsseler Jubelpark, ist Teil der K\u00f6niglichen Museen f\u00fcr Kunst und Geschichte und bietet einen umfassenden und vielseitigen \u00dcberblick \u00fcber die Geschichte von den Hochkulturen der Antike bis hin zu den Kunststr\u00f6mungen der Gegenwart.\r\n\r\nAntike Sammlungen: \r\nDie antiken Sammlungen befassen sich mit den untergegangenen Hochkulturen von \u00c4gypten (Neuheit: das Grabmal von Nakht), Mesopotamien, Griechenland und Rom. Gezeigt werden au\u00dferdem die gro\u00dfen Kunststr\u00f6mungen Europas vom 10. Jahrhundert bis heute. Wandteppiche, Altaraufs\u00e4tze, Spitze, Goldschmiedekunst und Porzellan geh\u00f6ren zu den kostbaren H\u00f6hepunkten der Ausstellung.\r\n\r\nVon Mikronesien bis Amerika: \r\nDie nicht-europ\u00e4ischen Werke laden ihrerseits auf eine Reise ein: nach Mikronesien, Polynesien, Indien, S\u00fcdostasien, China und ins pr\u00e4kolumbische Amerika. In den eindrucksvollen Arch\u00e4ologie-S\u00e4len wird der Geschichte der Region von der Vorgeschichte bis zur Epoche der Merowinger neues Leben eingehaucht.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Museo Arte & Historia","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@mrah.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 14","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Situato nel cuore del complesso del Cinquantenario, il Mus\u00e9e du Cinquantenaire vi invita a viaggiatore attraverso i continenti dalla Preistoria al XX secolo. \r\n\r\n\r\nLe sue ricche collezioni sono suddivise in quattro grandi sezioni :\r\n\r\n- L'Antichit\u00e0 dove sono presentate le grandi civilt\u00e0 scomparse dell'Egitto, della Mesopotamia, della Grecia e di Roma.\r\n- Le Arti decorative europee dove scoprire le correnti artistiche dal X secolo ai giorni nostri.\r\n- Le Civilt\u00e0 non europee che invitano al viaggio: India, Sudest asiatico, Cina, America precolombiana.\r\n- L'archeologia nazionale per rivivere il passato delle nostre regioni, dalla Preistoria al periodo merovingio.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Museo de Arte e Historia","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@mrah.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 14","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Ad\u00e9ntrate en este edificio hist\u00f3rico, uno de los mayores museos de B\u00e9lgica erigido por el anterior rey belga Leopoldo II. Descubre una gran cantidad de objetos desde la prehistoria hasta la antig\u00fcedad y de las artes aplicadas europeas hasta una amplia colecci\u00f3n de arte no europea. Explora todo, incluyendo las interesantes exposiciones temporales, conferencias y otras actividades. Desafortunadamente, la p\u00e1gina web no es tan amplia como para mostrar toda nuestra colecci\u00f3n, compuesta por miles de tesoros del arte y objetos hist\u00f3ricos. Sin embargo, esperamos que nos visites y disfrutes descubriendo o redescubriendo el inmenso patrimonio que gestionamos y exhibimos. De hecho, para nosotros el arte y la historia no son muerte y temas pasados, si no una viva y constante fuente de inspiraci\u00f3n y diversi\u00f3n.\r\n\r\nEl Museo de Arte e Historia es parte de los Museos Reales de Arte e Historia(MRAH), que incluye el Museo de Instrumentos Musicales(MIM), la Puerta de Hal y los Museos del Lejano Oriente(recientemente cerrado por renovaciones).\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Museu de Arte e Hist\u00f3ria (MRAH)","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@mrah.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 15","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Da arqueologia nacional \u00e0s artes decorativas europeias, passando pela antiguidade cl\u00e1ssica e pelas civiliza\u00e7\u00f5es n\u00e3o europeias, embarque numa fascinante viagem atrav\u00e9s da arte e da hist\u00f3ria num edif\u00edcio magn\u00edfico criado por L\u00e9opold II no parque do Cinquenten\u00e1rio em Bruxelas.\r\n\r\n-  Museu do Cinquenten\u00e1rio muda de pele e torna-se o Museu de Arte e Hist\u00f3ria!\r\n-  Museu do Cinquenten\u00e1rio desenvolveu um trabalho de reflex\u00e3o sobre a sua imagem. Este resultou numa campanha de reorganiza\u00e7\u00e3o global da institui\u00e7\u00e3o. Come\u00e7ou assim uma reconquista museogr\u00e1fica: a decis\u00e3o de organizar exposi\u00e7\u00f5es tempor\u00e1rias baseadas nas pr\u00f3prias cole\u00e7\u00f5es do museu e de renovar progressivamente as salas permanentes, come\u00e7ando pelo armaz\u00e9m Wolfers, que foi a primeira etapa de uma s\u00e9rie de outras renova\u00e7\u00f5es (salas Egito, salas s\u00e9culos XIX e XX, maqueta de Roma\u2026) que atingem rapidamente a sua velocidade de cruzeiro. O\r\n- Museu de Arte e Hist\u00f3ria pertence aos Museus Reais de Arte e da Hist\u00f3ria, que englobam, para al\u00e9m deste, o MIM (Museu dos Instrumentos Musicais), a Porta de Hal e os Museus do Extremo Oriente, atualmente encerrados.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e Art & Histoire (MRAH)","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@mrah.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 15","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":{"list":[9],"translations":{"fr":["Quartier europ\u00e9en"],"nl":["Europese wijk"],"en":["European Quarter"]}},"zones":{"list":[22],"translations":{"fr":["Est"],"nl":["Oost"],"en":["East"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":12,"location":{"lat":50.83935087,"lon":4.3917188},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-05-18T01:36:45+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:13+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":61,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e Art & Histoire (MRAH)","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@mrah.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 15","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"De l'arch\u00e9ologie nationale aux arts d\u00e9coratifs europ\u00e9ens en passant par l'Antiquit\u00e9 classique et les civilisations non europ\u00e9ennes, embarquez pour un fascinant voyage \u00e0 travers l'art et l'histoire dans un magnifique b\u00e2timent, cr\u00e9\u00e9 par L\u00e9opold II dans le parc du Cinquantenaire \u00e0 Bruxelles.\r\n\r\nLe Mus\u00e9e Art & Histoire fait partie des Mus\u00e9es royaux d\u2019Art et d\u2019Histoire, appellation qui chapeaute, outre le Mus\u00e9e Art & Histoire, le mim (Mus\u00e9e des Instruments de Musique), la Porte de Hal et les Mus\u00e9es d\u2019Extr\u00eame-Orient actuellement ferm\u00e9s. ","description_print":"Le Mus\u00e9e du Cinquantenaire illustre les activit\u00e9s humaines et artistiques des cinq continents \u2013 hormis l\u2019Afrique noire \u2013, de la Pr\u00e9histoire \u00e0 nos jours. Les collections remplissent quatre b\u00e2timents et sont regroup\u00e9es en quatre d\u00e9partements: l\u2019Antiquit\u00e9, les civilisations extra-europ\u00e9ennes, l\u2019arch\u00e9ologie nationale et les arts d\u00e9coratifs europ\u00e9ens.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Museum Kunst & Geschiedenis (KMKG)","address_street_name":"Jubelpark","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@kmkg.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 14","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Jubelpark","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Maak een wereldreis door de geschiedenis! Wandel van prehistorische vuistbijlen naar Egyptische mummies. Snuistert tussen betoverende glas en zet een stap achteruit om de indrukwekkende Brusselse wandtapijten te bekijken. Ga de oosterse toer op tussen de Aziatische boeddha\u2019s en steek de Atlantische Oceaan over om Kuifjes \u2018beeldje met het gebroken oor\u2019. En dan is er nog de mooie collectie van Belgische art nouveau\u2026 U komt ogen en oren te kort!\r\n\r\nHet Museum Kunst & Geschiedenis maakt deel uit van de Koninklijke Musea voor Kunst en Geschiedenis (KMKG) die ook het Muziekinstrumentenmuseum (MIM), de Hallepoort en de Musea van het Verre Oosten (gesloten voor renovatie) bundelen.","description_print":"Het Jubelparkmuseum kan bogen op een imposante collectie kunstschatten en archeologische vondsten afkomstig uit de vijf continenten \u2013 met uitzondering van Zwart-Afrika \u2013 van de prehistorie tot op heden. De verzamelingen vullen vier gebouwen en zijn ingedeeld in evenveel departementen: Oudheid (het Nabije Oosten, Egypte, Griekenland, Rome en Byzantium), Niet-Europese Beschavingen (Islam, Azi\u00eb, Polynesi\u00eb & Micronesi\u00eb en Amerika), Nationale Archeologie en Europese Sierkunsten.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Art & History Museum (RMAH)","address_street_name":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"info@mrah.be","website":"https:\/\/www.artandhistory.museum","phone_contact":"+32 2 741 73 31","phone_booking":"+32 2 741 72 14","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Parc du Cinquantenaire","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"Step inside this historic building, one of the biggest museums in Belgium and erected by former Belgian King Leopold II. Discover a wealth of artefacts from prehistoric times over antiquity and the European applied arts to a vast collection of non-European art. Explore what's on, including interesting temporary exhibitions, lectures and various other activities. Unfortunately, the website does not extend to giving you a full viewing of our collection, comprising thousands of art treasures and historical objects. However, we hope that you will come and visit us and enjoy discovering or rediscovering the immense heritage that we manage and display. To us, indeed, art and history are not dead and dusty subjects, but very much alive and a constant source of inspiration and enjoyment.\r\n\r\nThe Art & History Museum is part of the Royal Museums of Art and History (RMAH) th