ngepast toilet"],"en":["Accessible to people with intellectual disabilities","Facilities for blind and partially-sighted persons","Facilities for deaf and hearing-impaired people","Assistance dogs","Accessible parking","Accessible to pedestrians with mobility aids","Adapted toilet"]}},"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2022-04-08T16:05:07+02:00","published_at":"2022-04-08T15:48:47+02:00","backoffice_id":251240,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"theatre","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":1.2599210498949},{"id":529834,"date_start":"2022-05-20","date_end":"2022-05-22","date_next":"2022-05-20","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":70,"translations":{"fr":"Foire & salon","nl":"Beurzen & salons","en":"Fairs and shows"}},"others":{}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr","en","nl"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Collectible 2022 - Design Fair","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"La foire internationale COLLECTIBLE, d\u00e9di\u00e9e au design de collection du 21e si\u00e8cle, revient au Vanderborght Building du 20 au 22 mai 2022. Pour ses cinq ans, la plateforme qui rassemble galeries \u00e9tablies et \u00e9mergentes, designers et studios de design ind\u00e9pendants lancera The Editors, un espace ouvert et visionnaire consacr\u00e9 aux labels de design pionniers. \u00c0 la crois\u00e9e de l\u2019art et du design, COLLECTIBLE permet tout \u00e0 la fois la d\u00e9couverte et l\u2019acquisition de pi\u00e8ces uniques et d'\u00e9ditions limit\u00e9es ainsi que des \u00e9changes autour de projets in\u00e9dits. Cette ann\u00e9e, la section Curated pr\u00e9sentera E S C A P I S M, un espace pens\u00e9 par le collectionneur et curateur Berry Dijkstra, bas\u00e9 \u00e0 Rotterdam et en parall\u00e8le TENSION!, la section Curated de 2021, imagin\u00e9e par la curatrice, \u00e9crivaine et entrepreneuse Julia Haney Monta\u00f1ez bas\u00e9e \u00e0 New York, sera d\u00e9voil\u00e9e pour la premi\u00e8re fois en physique avec des nouveaut\u00e9s.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":"http:\/\/agenda.brussels\/fr\/529834\/collectible-2022-design-fair\/shop","website":"https:\/\/collectible.design\/","email":"info@collectible.design","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/fr\/detail\/id\/529834.html"},"nl":{"name":"Collectible 2022 - Design Fair","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"COLLECTIBLE, de internationale beurs gewijd aan collectief design van de 21ste eeuw, keert terug naar het Vanderborghtgebouw van 20 tot 22 mei 2022. Het platform dat gevestigde en opkomende galerijen, ontwerpers en onafhankelijke designstudio's samenbrengt, lanceert voor het vijfde jaar The Editors, een open en visionaire ruimte gewijd aan vernieuwende designlabels. Op het kruispunt van kunst en design biedt COLLECTIBLE de mogelijkheid om unieke stukken en gelimiteerde uitgaven te ontdekken en te verkrijgen, maar ook om nieuwe projecten onder de aandacht te brengen. Dit jaar zal de beurs twee gecureerde segmenten voorstellen. De Curated section E S C A P I S M, doordacht door de verzamelaar en curator Berry Dijkstra uit Rotterdam. Daarnaast TENSION!, doordacht door de curator, schrijver en ondernemer Julia Haney Monta\u00f1ez uit New York, deze Curated section van 2021 wordt voor de eerste keer onthuld met nieuwigheden.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":"http:\/\/agenda.brussels\/nl\/529834\/collectible-2022-design-fair\/shop","website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/nl\/detail\/id\/529834.html"},"en":{"name":"Collectible 2022 - Design Fair","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Exclusively dedicated to 21-century cutting edge design, COLLECTIBLE is an international fair that brings together renowned and emerging designers and galleries. This year, the fifth edition of COLLECTIBLE will take place at the Vanderborght Building, in the heart of Brussels from 20 to 22 May 2022. The pioneering platform will offer its visitors a fresh selection of unique and exclusive pieces available only in limited editions. More novelties await with the launch of The Editors, a new platform dedicated to visionary and niche design labels. This year\u2019s Curated section presents E S C A P I S M, imagined by Rotterdam-based collector and curator Berry Dijkstra, alongside an iteration of the 2021 Curated section, TENSION!, conceived by New York-based curator, writer and entrepreneur Julia Haney Monta\u00f1ez will be physically accessible for the first time with new additions.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":"http:\/\/agenda.brussels\/en\/529834\/collectible-2022-design-fair\/shop","website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/en\/detail\/id\/529834.html"},"de":{"name":"Collectible 2022","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/de\/detail\/id\/529834.html"},"it":{"name":"Collectible 2022","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/it\/detail\/id\/529834.html"},"sp":{"name":"Collectible 2022","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/sp\/detail\/id\/529834.html"},"pt":{"name":"Collectible 2022","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/pt\/detail\/id\/529834.html"},"cn":{"name":"Collectible 2022","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/cn\/detail\/id\/529834.html"}},"place":{"id":251380,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Espace Vanderborght","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ecuyer","address_street_number":"50","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ecuyer, 50","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Propri\u00e9t\u00e9 de la Ville de Bruxelles, cet \u00e9difice \u00e0 la large vitrine se dresse en plein centre de Bruxelles, \u00e0 deux pas des c\u00e9l\u00e8bres Galeries royales Saint-Hubert et \u00e0 peine plus loin de la Grand-Place. Il occupe un espace impressionnant de 6 000 m\u00e8tres carr\u00e9s de surface utile, r\u00e9partis sur 5 \u00e9tages.\r\n\r\nConstruit au profit des \u00ab Nouveaux \u00c9tablissements Vanderborght Fr\u00e8res \u00bb, n\u00e9goce en mobilier (tapis, bibelots, mobilier de jardin, literie, etc.), l\u2019\u00e9difice est con\u00e7u par un tandem habitu\u00e9 \u00e0 travailler ensemble : les architectes Govaerts et Van Vaerenbergh, auteurs \u00e9galement de la maison d\u2019Alice et David van Buren \u2014 actuel mus\u00e9e van Buuren. Le chantier, entam\u00e9 en 1932, prend fin en 1935. De style moderniste, la conception de l\u2019immeuble est d\u00e9nu\u00e9e de tout ornement et privil\u00e9gie la fonction.\r\n\r\nRemarquable par ses larges vitrines permettant une grande visibilit\u00e9, chaque \u00e9tage est constitu\u00e9 d\u2019un grand un plateau de b\u00e9ton modulable, gr\u00e2ce \u00e0 un syst\u00e8me de cloisons coulissantes sur rail. Le b\u00e2timent se distingue encore par ses terrasses, lieu d\u2019exposition des meubles de jardin mais aussi de d\u00e9tente \u2014 on peut y prendre un th\u00e9 \u00e0 l\u2019\u00e9poque ! Le magasin tombe en faillite en 1980.\r\n\r\nLes Mus\u00e9es Royaux des Beaux-Arts ont envisag\u00e9 d\u2019y transf\u00e9rer leurs collections d\u2019art moderne et contemporain, mais le projet restera sans suite.\r\n\r\nLe lieu abrite aujourd\u2019hui de nombreuses expositions, principalement centr\u00e9es sur l\u2019art contemporain. Trois grands rendez-vous sont ainsi programm\u00e9s chaque ann\u00e9e :\r\n-\tCarte de Visite ARTopenKUNST en f\u00e9vrier, une expo d\u00e9di\u00e9e aux artistes amateurs et professionnels qui habitent ou travaillent sur la Ville de Bruxelles. Plus de 200 artistes envahissent tout le b\u00e2timent pendant un weekend. http:\/\/cartedevisite.brussels\/ \r\n-\tThe Independent en avril, une foire d\u2019art contemporain newyorkaise qui a pos\u00e9 ses valises \u00e0 Bruxelles. http:\/\/independenthq.com\/\r\n-\tStrokar en mai, une exposition d\u00e9di\u00e9e au Street Art et \u00e0 la photographie qui rassemble des artistes bruxellois et internationaux. http:\/\/strokar.be\/ \r\n\r\nPar ailleurs d\u2019autres expositions non r\u00e9currentes y trouvent place, ouvertes au plus grand nombre et proposant un prix tr\u00e8s accessible.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Vanderborghtgebouw","address_street_name":"Schildknaapsstraat","address_street_number":"50","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Schildknaapsstraat, 50","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Dit gebouw, dat eigendom is van de stad Brussel, ligt in het hartje van Brussel, op een steenworp van de beroemde Koninklijke Sint-Hubertusgalerijen en de Grote Markt. Het neemt een indrukwekkende 6.000 vierkante meter vloeroppervlak in beslag, verdeeld over 5 verdiepingen.\r\n\r\nIndertijd gebouwd voor een meubelhandelaar (tapijten, snuisterijen, tuinmeubelen, beddengoed, enz.), \"Nouveaux \u00c9tablissements Vanderborght Fr\u00e8res\", werd het gebouw ontworpen door een team dat gewend was om samen te werken: architecten Govaerts en Van Vaerenbergh, de ontwerpers van het huis van Alice en David van Buren - nu het van Buuren Museum. De bouwwerkzaamheden, die in 1932 begonnen, eindigden in 1935. Eigen aan de modernistische stijl is het ontwerp van het gebouw verstoken van ornamenten en benadrukt het de functie.\r\n\r\nElke verdieping bestaat uit een groot modulair betonnen plateau, dankzij een systeem van verschuifbare scheidingswanden op rails, met opmerkelijk grote ramen die een hoge zichtbaarheid mogelijk maken. Het gebouw kenmerkt zich ook nog door zijn terrassen, de plek waar het tuinmeubilair werd tentoongesteld en waar men ook kon ontspannen (indertijd kon je daar thee drinken). De winkel ging in 1980 failliet.\r\n\r\nDe Koninklijke Musea voor Schone Kunsten hebben overwogen om hun collecties moderne en hedendaagse kunst hierheen over te brengen, maar het project werd niet voortgezet.\r\n\r\nVandaag de dag worden er vele tentoonstellingen georganiseerd, voornamelijk gericht op hedendaagse kunst. Elk jaar staan er drie grote evenementen op het programma:\r\n- ARTopenKUNST in februari, een tentoonstelling gewijd aan amateur- en professionele kunstenaars die in de stad Brussel wonen of werken. Meer dan 200 kunstenaars vallen een weekend lang het hele gebouw binnen. http:\/\/cartedevisite.brussels\/ \r\n- The Independent in april, een New Yorkse beurs voor hedendaagse kunst die zich in Brussel heeft gevestigd. http:\/\/independenthq.com\/\r\n- Strokar in mei, een tentoonstelling gewijd aan Street Art en fotografie die Brussel en internationale kunstenaars samenbrengt. http:\/\/strokar.be\/ \r\n\r\nDaarnaast herbergt het gebouw nog vele andere, niet-wederkerende tentoonstellingen, die openstaan voor het grote publiek aan een zeer toegankelijke prijs.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Espace Vanderborght","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ecuyer","address_street_number":"50","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ecuyer, 50","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"Owned by the City of Brussels, this building with a large shop window stands in the centre of Brussels, only a stone\u2019s throw from the Grand Place. It occupies an impressive 6,000 m\u00b2 of space spread over 5 stories.\r\n\r\nBuilt for the \u201cNouveaux \u00c9tablissements Vanderborght Fr\u00e8res\u201d, who traded in household products like carpets, knick-knacks, garden furniture, bedding, etc., the building was designed by architects Govaerts and Van Vaerenbergh, who were used to working together, having previously collaborated on the house of Alice and David van Buren, now the van Buren Museum. The building works, which began in 1932, were completed in 1935. Built in a modernist style, the building did away with ornamental elements, favouring function over appearance.\r\n\r\nWith remarkable large shop front windows that allow for greater visibility, each story is made up of one large concrete floorplan that can be easily modified thanks to a system of sliding partition walls on tracks. Other stand-out features of this building are its terraces, which served as exhibition spaces for the company\u2019s garden furniture back in the day, but also spots to relax and enjoy a cup of tea. The store went bankrupt in 1980.\r\n\r\nThe Royal Fine Arts Museums of Belgium once thought of moving their collections into the Vanderborght building, but the project never took off.\r\n\r\nThe venue today welcomes many exhibitions, mainly centred around contemporary art. Three major events are organised every year:\r\n-\tCarte de Visite ARTopenKUNST in February: an exhibition dedicated to amateur and professional artists living or working in the City of Brussels. More than 200 artists take over the building for a whole weekend. http:\/\/cartedevisite.brussels\/ \r\n-\tThe Independent in April: a contemporary art fair from New Year has set up shop in Brussels. http:\/\/independenthq.com\/\r\n-\tStrokar in May: an exhibition dedicated to street art and photography that gathers artists from Brussels and further afield. http:\/\/strokar.be\/ \r\n\r\nFurthermore, other, non-recurrent exhibitions also take place in the Vanderborght building and are open to all at a reasonable price.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Espace Vanderborght","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ecuyer","address_street_number":"50","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ecuyer, 50","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Espace Vanderborght","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ecuyer","address_street_number":"50","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ecuyer, 50","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Espace Vanderborght","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ecuyer","address_street_number":"50","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de l'Ecuyer, 50","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Espace Vanderborght","address_street_name":"Rue de l'Ecuyer","address_stree